## Hard Constraints (Do NOT)

1. Do not touch production config (`.env.production`, prod profiles, prod manifests)
2. Do not modify third-party / external API adapter code without explicit approval
3. Do not modify money / billing / commission logic outside the full `codex-handoff` flow
4. Do not force-push to `main` or any protected branch
5. Do not delete migration files
6. Do not install new dependencies without explicit confirmation

## Decision Boundaries

Owner sign-off required, not agent autonomy: commercial terms, visual design beyond existing patterns, user-facing copy in new languages, anything touching real production data.

## Collaboration Workflow

This project uses the **`codex-handoff` skill**: Claude plans and writes a spec, a Claude subagent implements, Codex reviews (`/codex:adversarial-review`). The main agent never edits source or runs verify itself, and implementation and review are never the same model — if Codex is unavailable, the review waits.

Load the skill for any non-trivial coding task. Specs live in `.agent/specs/`, review reports in `.agent/reviews/`; both are committed as design history.
